From: Raven Contributors <raven@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] Honor configured update threading and synchronize clone writes

The ROS executable unconditionally overrides multi_threading_subs after parsing.
Respect the requested synchronous mode instead. With asynchronous updates,
State::margtimestep() can run during clone insertion or ZUPT clone removal;
its reader lock must also protect those writes. Normal marginalization already
uses this mutex. A captured A55 core stopped in std::_Rb_tree_increment while
the IMU callback traversed this map during a camera update.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Raven Contributors <raven@localhost>

--- a/ov_msckf/src/run_subscribe_msckf.cpp
+++ b/ov_msckf/src/run_subscribe_msckf.cpp
@@ -83,7 +83,6 @@
   // Create our VIO system
   VioManagerOptions params;
   params.print_and_load(parser);
-  params.use_multi_threading_subs = true;
   sys = std::make_shared<VioManager>(params);
 #if ROS_AVAILABLE == 1
   viz = std::make_shared<ROS1Visualizer>(nh, sys);
--- a/ov_msckf/src/state/StateHelper.cpp
+++ b/ov_msckf/src/state/StateHelper.cpp
@@ -596,7 +596,11 @@
   }
 
   // Append the new clone to our clone vector
-  state->_clones_IMU[state->_timestamp] = pose;
+  {
+    // margtimestep() reads this map from the IMU callback.
+    std::lock_guard<std::mutex> lock(state->_mutex_state);
+    state->_clones_IMU[state->_timestamp] = pose;
+  }
 
   // If we are doing time calibration, then our clones are a function of the time offset
   // Logic is based on Mingyang Li and Anastasios I. Mourikis paper:
--- a/ov_msckf/src/update/UpdaterZeroVelocity.cpp
+++ b/ov_msckf/src/update/UpdaterZeroVelocity.cpp
@@ -320,7 +320,11 @@
     // finally update and remove the old clone
     StateHelper::EKFUpdate(state, Hx_order, H, res, R);
     StateHelper::marginalize(state, state->_clones_IMU.at(time1_cam));
-    state->_clones_IMU.erase(time1_cam);
+    {
+      // Use the same lock as margtimestep() for every clone-map mutation.
+      std::lock_guard<std::mutex> lock(state->_mutex_state);
+      state->_clones_IMU.erase(time1_cam);
+    }
   }
 
   // Finally return
